"Take the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God"

Ephesians chapter 6 verse 17

This verse was authored by God, written through the Apostle Paul to the church in Ephesus during his imprisonment in Rome


We are here together to train in becoming capable and dangerous soldiers of Christ Jesus

We wear the full armor of God

We train the blade so we may wield the sword of the spirit with precision and strength


--> Point 1: We are in a spiritual war. No a war of flesh and blood, a spiritual war fought for the souls of humans

If you read the 66 books of the bible and look around you, it's clear to see we are in a spirtual war. If you don't believe that is true, this is not the right podcast for you

When you see that fact to be true and want to defend and contend for our Lord Jesus Christ, please return



--> Point 2: We serve a King who is worthy to be served

An all powerful King. A strong King. A powerful King. Lord of all Lords. A victorious King that gave his blood to save us from sin and eternity in hell

We owe our Lord our lives

We serve the Lord Jesus Christ. We are not slaves to men, but servants of Christ who removed our bonds





--> Point 3: To truly serve God means to win souls.

That is how we bear fruit for our King

We capture souls from the Kingdom of darkness



--> Point 4: Charles Spurgeon said that Christians are soldiers on enemy territory, always needing to be on watch and constantly contending

Not contending with flesh and blood, but with far worse foes. Namely, the forces of spiritual wickedness



--> Point 5: We train to be ready for conflict

We read the word daily. We train our minds and bodies daily to be mentally and physically strong

The word is the short sword of the spiritual battlefield

The weapon required 



--> Point 6: The soldier of Christ Jesus is a serving man

He forfeits pursuits of his own pleasure for the pursuit of doing damage to the kingdom of darkness

We discipline our earthly desires and find supreme pleasure in serving our Lord



--> Point 7: He fears God and obeys his commands

In Ecclesiastes 12:13, God says through the preacher "Fear God and keep his commandments, for this is the whole duty of man"

A good soldier of Christ Jesus upholds that clear command







Father, we bow our hearts to you and pray that you would guide us to become able warriors of your heavenly kingdom

In Jesus name, amen

